# ---- build tree -----------------------------------------------------------
build/

# ---- compiler intermediates ----------------------------------------------
*.o
*.d
*.ll
*.bc

# ---- binaries from running `ovc <file>.ov` in place ------------------------
# (ovc writes the executable next to the source, with the extension removed)
examples/chatbot/chatbot

# ---- chatbot persistent memory --------------------------------------------
# Written at runtime by examples/chatbot/chatbot_rag.ov; it holds conversation
# history, so it is state, not source.
examples/chatbot/chatbot_memory.json
examples/chatbot/chatbot_rag_memory.json
tests/gemini_ask
/hello
/hello_world

# ---- editors and OS -------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store

# ---- vs code extension -----------------------------------------------------
# node_modules and dist are build products; bin/ovyth-lsp is built by
# `make lsp` at package time and vendored into the .vsix.
editors/vscode/node_modules/
editors/vscode/dist/
editors/vscode/bin/
editors/vscode/*.vsix

# ---- local AI-assistant guidance ---------------------------------------------
# AGENTS.md is the working set of rules for the AI coding assistant on this
# machine. It is deliberately not tracked: CONTRIBUTING.md is the repository's
# contributor guidance, and keeping the two separate means a local experiment
# in agent instructions can never land as project policy by accident.
AGENTS.md

# WORKLOG.md is the running session log for the same reason: a working note
# for whoever is in the tree today, not project history. CHANGELOG.md is the
# tracked record of what shipped.
WORKLOG.md

# LOW-LEVEL-AUDIT.md is a working analysis document for the same reason. If
# the audit's conclusions are accepted, the decisions that survive belong in
# CHANGELOG.md and the new APIs in docs/USAGE.md -- both tracked.
LOW-LEVEL-AUDIT.md

# ---- scratch --------------------------------------------------------------
*.tmp
# compiled test binaries (an `ovc x.ov` with no -o writes ./x)
/0*
/1*
/2*
